# PART 6 — DATA MANAGEMENT & PRIVACY

## 11. First Release Storage

The first prototype must use browser localStorage.

Requirements:

- Automatically save changes.
- Retain data after browser refresh.
- Provide manual JSON export.
- Provide JSON import.
- Provide CSV export of travel records.
- Validate imported files before replacing existing data.
- Warn before deleting all records.
- Provide a sample/demo dataset that can be reset.

No account registration or authentication is required in the first release.

No cloud database is required.

No real passport numbers, immigration account credentials or sensitive identity documents should be requested.

Clearly inform users that localStorage data is browser-specific and may be lost if browser data is cleared.

