# PART 8 — ACCEPTANCE CRITERIA

## 13. Minimum Functional Requirements

The first draft is considered successful when:

1. A user can create and edit an immigration profile.
2. A user can add, edit and delete travel records.
3. All travel records persist after browser refresh.
4. The application correctly calculates Naturalisation whole-day absences.
5. The application can calculate the maximum absence within the configured ILR rolling 12-month windows.
6. The application distinguishes ILR and Naturalisation calculations.
7. The dashboard displays all three absence metrics.
8. The calendar displays travel history.
9. The timeline displays estimated immigration milestones.
10. The Travel Simulator can calculate the impact of a proposed trip without permanently changing the original records.
11. Invalid and incomplete records are clearly identified.
12. Users can export and restore their data.
13. The application works on desktop and mobile.
14. All important calculations have automated tests.
15. No AI-generated legal eligibility decision is displayed.

## 14. Required Calculation Test Cases

The following cases must be implemented as automated tests.

| Test | Expected behaviour |
|---|---|
| Same-day UK departure and return | 0 Naturalisation absence days |
| Departure 1 June, return 10 June | 8 Naturalisation absence days |
| Departure 31 December, return 3 January | 2 Naturalisation absence days |
| Leap-year February | Correct calendar arithmetic |
| Exactly 180 ILR absence days | Within normal threshold |
| 181 ILR absence days | Normal threshold exceeded |
| Exactly 450 Naturalisation absence days | Within normal threshold |
| 451 Naturalisation absence days | Normal threshold exceeded |
| Exactly 90 final-12-month days | Within normal threshold |
| 91 final-12-month days | Normal threshold exceeded |
| Two overlapping trips | Validation warning |
| Missing return date | Incomplete record |
| Travel simulation | Original records remain unchanged |
| No travel records | Display insufficient data / no records, not an unqualified legal Pass |

Additional tests must cover overlapping rolling windows, leap days, calendar-month boundaries and trips crossing qualifying-period boundaries.

